cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use JALEBI in your research, please cite it as below, together with HITRAN/HITEMP, emcee and the methods you used (see the README references)."
title: "JALEBI: JWST Analysis of Line Emission with Bayesian Inference"
abstract: "Simultaneous LTE slab fitting of the molecular emission in JWST/MIRI-MRS spectra of protoplanetary disks, with continuum estimation, automatic molecule detection, parallel MCMC (emitting areas sampled, profiled or marginalised) and an interactive web app; line maps, velocity maps, channel maps, PV cuts and region spectra of IFU cubes; rotation diagrams of H2, CO, OH and H2O with extinction, ortho-to-para ratio and optical depth."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baskaran
    given-names: Shridharan
    email: shridharan.baskaran@tifr.res.in
    affiliation: "Tata Institute of Fundamental Research"
version: 0.17.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/shridharanbaskaran/jalebi"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - JWST
  - MIRI
  - protoplanetary disks
  - LTE slab models
  - infrared spectroscopy
  - MCMC
  - IFU line maps
  - rotation diagrams
